        "For eleven years, the bus stop outside the post office in the hill town of Kirkby had no bench. The old wooden one had rotted and been taken away, and nobody had replaced it. Most passengers did not mind; they were young enough to stand for ten minutes. But Daniel Moore, a sixteen-year-old who rode the bus to school every morning, noticed that some passengers did mind. An elderly woman with a walking stick leaned against the post-office wall each day, and a man who had recently had an operation sat on the edge of a flowerpot because there was nowhere else.",
